== logout in a non-login shell is refused:
1:1: error: Builtin `logout`: Cannot use 'logout' in a non-login shell.
     1 |  logout
       |  ^~~~~~
note: `exit` may be used instead.
rc=1
== logout with a non-numeric operand is a located error:
1:1: error: Builtin `logout`: Cannot use 'logout' in a non-login shell.
     1 |  logout abc
       |  ^~~~~~~~~~
note: `exit` may be used instead.
rc=1
== logout runs the EXIT action with its operand:
body
action-ran
rc=5
== bare logout keeps the status the action found:
action-ran
rc=0
== an external last command in the action keeps the logout status:
external-last
rc=6
== an exit inside the action replaces the logout status:
head
rc=9
